WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:01.290
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.310
Hi, you guys.
嘿，你们好。

3
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.230
We are still on vacation.
我们还在度假中。

4
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.410
It's just a wonderful time to be home and with our families.
能回家和家人待在一起真是太棒了。

5
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.930
But you know, we always like to pop in and say hi.
但你们知道，我们总喜欢抽空露个面，打个招呼。

6
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.810
It is almost a new year.
马上就要到新的一年了。

7
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:13.770
2022.
2022年。

8
00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:15.630
OMG.
天哪。

9
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:16.950
I know.
我知道。

10
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:17.890
Where does the time go?
时间都去哪儿了？

11
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:18.790
I don't know.
我不知道。

12
00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.370
I don't know.
我也不知道。

13
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:24.490
Well, listen, Ange, I thought it would be fun, since we're approaching a new year,
好吧，听着，安吉，我想既然快到新年了，做点有趣的事应该不错，

14
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:30.410
to do a little deep dive on the history of New Year's.
比如深入了解一下新年的历史。

15
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.570
Oh, no way.
哦，不会吧。

16
00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:32.210
Yes.
是的。

17
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.330
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

18
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.310
I'm getting a cup of tea.
我去泡杯茶。

19
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.430
I'm settling in.
我准备好听了。

20
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:35.890
Okay.
好的。

21
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.670
So, here's what I found out from my three to four articles that I Googled.
那么，这是我从谷歌搜索的三四篇文章里了解到的内容。

22
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:49.130
In America, we celebrate the new year with a celebration that sort of encompasses December 31st into January 1St.
在美国，我们庆祝新年的方式涵盖了从12月31日到1月1日这段时间。

23
00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:49.530
Yes.
没错。

24
00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.910
That's our big New Year's celebration.
那是我们盛大的新年庆祝活动。

25
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.610
And you can take down your tree after that.
在那之后你就可以拆掉圣诞树了。

26
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.790
Oh, we can't?
哦，我们不能拆吗？

27
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.010
That's what I'm telling you.
我就是这个意思。

28
00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.850
I leave mine up until after New Year's.
我的树一直留到新年过后。

29
00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.730
Well, we usually do, too.
嗯，我们通常也是。

30
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.470
But I'm just telling you out there, it's okay if it's up after New Year's.
但我只是想告诉大家，新年过后树还没拆也没关系。

31
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.390
Have you ever had your tree up until, like, February?
你有没有试过把树一直留到二月份？

32
00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:06.190
No.
没有。

33
00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:06.750
How late?
最晚到什么时候？

34
00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.310
Like, what's the latest?
就是说，最晚是什么时候？

35
00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.550
Have you met my husband?
你见过我丈夫吗？

36
00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.710
It's coming down on January 2nd.
1月2号就得拆掉。

37
00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.490
He would pack it up on the 26th if I didn't stop him.
如果我不拦着他，他26号就会把它打包收起来。

38
00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:15.590
That is true.
那是真的。

39
00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

40
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.050
All right.
好吧。

41
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:23.610
Well, listen, the earliest recorded New Year's festivities date back 4,000 years to ancient Babylon.
听着，最早有记载的新年庆祝活动可以追溯到4000年前的古巴比伦。

42
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:32.150
However, they did not celebrate on December 31st, January 1st because the calendar wasn't sort of the same calendar.
不过，他们并不是在12月31日或1月1日庆祝，因为那时的历法和现在的不太一样。

43
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:40.690
They celebrated on the vernal equinox, and that is the day in late March when there is an equal amount of sunlight and darkness.
他们在春分那天庆祝，也就是三月下旬白天和黑夜时长相等的那一天。

44
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.890
That was their New Year?
那是他们的新年？

45
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.970
That was their New Year on that day.
那天就是他们的新年。

46
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.530
Babylon crazy.
巴比伦人真疯狂。

47
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:58.550
So, in general, civilizations around the world developed calendars that would pin the New Year either on, like, an agricultural event or on an astronomical event.
所以，总的来说，世界各地的文明所制定的历法，通常会将新年定在某个农业事件或天文事件上。

48
00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.170
Okay.
好的。

49
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:07.110
So, in Egypt, for example, the year began with the annual flooding of the Nile and the rising star Sirius.
比如在埃及，新的一年开始于尼罗河的年度洪水和天狼星的升起。

50
00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.050
Okay.
好的。

51
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:14.730
The first day of the Chinese New Year occurred with the second moon after the winter solstice.
农历新年出现在冬至后的第二个新月。

52
00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:15.410
Okay.
好的。

53
00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:23.850
The early Roman calendar consisted of 10 months and 304 days, and the New Year also began at the vernal equinox.
早期的罗马历法由10个月和304天组成，新年也是从春分开始的。

54
00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.130
But guess what happened?
但你猜怎么着？

55
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:25.650
What?
怎么了？

56
00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.850
Their calendar got out of sync with the sun.
他们的历法与太阳不同步了。

57
00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:29.790
Huh?
啊？

58
00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.490
Yeah.
是啊。

59
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:46.270
So, in order to realign the Roman calendar with the sun, Julius Caesar consulted with all these astronomers and mathematicians, and in the year 46 BC, he added 90 days to the year.
所以，为了让罗马历法与太阳重新对齐，尤利乌斯·凯撒咨询了所有的天文学家和数学家，并在公元前46年，给那一年增加了90天。

60
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.610
Can you imagine?
你能想象吗？

61
00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:48.790
Can you imagine?
你能想象吗？

62
00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.690
It's like, it's 46 BC.
就像是，当时是公元前46年。

63
00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.450
You feel like, what if you've had a tough year?
你可能会想，如果你那一年过得很艰难怎么办？

64
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:53.850
Yeah.
是啊。

65
00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.090
And you're like, it's almost over.
你觉得，这一年快要结束了。

66
00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.930
I mean, it's almost a new year.
我是说，快要到新年了。

67
00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.550
And then Julius Caesar is like, guys, we're going to add 90 days to the calendar.
然后尤利乌斯·凯撒说，伙计们，我们要给历法增加90天。

68
00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.710
You know what I can't stop thinking about is, how did they get the word out?
你知道我一直想的是什么吗，他们是怎么把消息传出去的？

69
00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:16.230
Because, like, let's just talk about, you know, for example, our kid's school, when there's something, like a soccer game changes, and the emails you get, and the texts you get.
因为，咱们就拿我们孩子的学校举例吧，当有什么变动，比如足球比赛时间改了，你会收到邮件和短信。

70
00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:20.550
But what if you're not on the text thread, and then you show up at soccer practice, and it's not that day?
但如果你没在短信群里，然后你去了足球训练场，结果那天根本没训练，怎么办？

71
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.770
How did they get the word out?
他们是怎么把消息传出去的？

72
00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:23.510
I don't know.
我不知道。

73
00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.950
I feel like people were showing up for work, and they're like, no, no, no, dude, dude, dude.
我觉得当时有人去上班，然后别人跟他说，不不不，伙计，伙计，伙计。

74
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.170
We got, like, 90 more days of vacay, like, or something.
我们还有90天的假期，或者类似的情况。

75
00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.630
They're like, no, no, no, no, no.
他们会说，不不不不不。

76
00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.130
Actually, that was last year.
其实那是去年了。

77
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.310
That was last year.
那是去年了。

78
00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:36.490
This is the new year.
这是新的一年。

79
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.530
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

80
00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:38.570
Yeah.
是啊。

81
00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.670
I mean, the Roman Empire was vaSt.
我是说，罗马帝国疆域辽阔。

82
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.190
How did they?
他们是怎么做到的？

83
00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.890
It was a lot of scrolls.
那得有多少卷轴啊。

84
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.070
A lot of scrolls in different languages.
各种语言的卷轴。

85
00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:50.750
Did they do, like, hear ye, hear ye, news on the street?
他们是不是搞了那种“听着，听着，街头新闻”之类的广播？

86
00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:51.090
Yeah.
是啊。

87
00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.130
90 more days of the year.
这一年又多了90天。

88
00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:53.770
Yeah.
是啊。

89
00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:54.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

90
00:03:55.090 --> 00:04:00.050
I just feel like there's someone that showed up to work, and, you know, they were, like, thinking it was one year, but it was the other year.
我只是觉得肯定有人去上班了，然后，你知道，他们以为是这一年，结果其实是那一年。

91
00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.190
I think there was some confusion.
我觉得肯定会有一些混乱。

92
00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.970
I mean, can you imagine the paperwork problems?
我是说，你能想象那些文书工作会有多麻烦吗？

93
00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:04.470
I don't know.
我不知道。

94
00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.170
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

95
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.510
He called this new calendar the Julian calendar.
他把这个新历法称为儒略历。

96
00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.550
Of course he would.
他当然会这么做。

97
00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.070
Of course.
当然了。

98
00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:14.910
And he also declared that January 1st would be the first day of the year.
他还宣布1月1日为一年的第一天。

99
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:23.770
He named January in honor of the god Janus, and he wanted to give Janus the honor of starting the whole calendar.
他以神雅努斯的名字命名了一月，并希望给予雅努斯开启整个历法的荣誉。

100
00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.310
So Julius Caesar is the reason why our New Year's in January?
所以尤利乌斯·凯撒就是我们新年在1月份的原因？

101
00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:27.850
Yeah.
是啊。

102
00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.710
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

103
00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.290
However, we don't use the Julian calendar anymore.
不过，我们现在已经不再使用儒略历了。

104
00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:39.450
We actually use the Gregorian calendar, but it's very similar, and they also consider January 1st the first day of the year.
我们实际上用的是格里高利历，也就是公历，但两者非常相似，它们也都把1月1日视为一年的第一天。

105
00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.490
So that's kind of how we got to January 1St.
所以这就是我们把1月1日定为元旦的由来。

106
00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:47.050
And in the United States, we have the Times Square ball drop.
在美国，我们有时代广场降球仪式。

107
00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.210
That's our big tradition.
那是我们的重大传统。

108
00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:49.210
Yes.
没错。

109
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.250
I worked it with Carson Daly one year.
有一年我还和卡森·戴利一起主持过。

110
00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.070
I can't believe you did that.
真不敢相信你做过这个。

111
00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:53.790
I froze my high knee off.
我当时冻得够呛。

112
00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:54.730
Was it so cold?
有那么冷吗？

113
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:54.950
It's so cold.
真的特别冷。

114
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:55.630
Yes.
是啊。

115
00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:56.790
I was so cold.
我当时冷坏了。

116
00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.350
It was really fun.
不过真的很有趣。

117
00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.270
I can't believe I did it because I hate being cold, but I did it.
我都不敢相信我居然做到了，因为我最怕冷了，但我还是坚持下来了。

118
00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.990
That is epic.
那太史诗级了。

119
00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:10.130
That is an epic-like thing as a performer, as a comedian, actor, to be part of that celebration.
作为一名表演者、喜剧演员或演员，能参与到那样的庆典中，确实是一件史诗般的事情。

120
00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.430
Live TV is terrifying.
直播电视节目太吓人了。

121
00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.290
Well, this tradition has been going on since 1907.
嗯，这个传统从1907年就开始了。

122
00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:23.410
The ball started as a 700-pound orb made out of iron, wood, and 100 light bulbs.
最初的球是一个重700磅的球体，由铁、木头和100个灯泡制成。

123
00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:24.970
Only 100.
才100个。

124
00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:30.350
Now it's like the Griswolds-like house in that Christmas Vacation movie.
现在的球就像电影《疯狂圣诞假期》里格里斯沃尔德家那栋房子一样。

125
00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.230
It is now 12 feet in diameter.
它现在的直径有12英尺。

126
00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.630
It is 12,000 pounds.
重达12000磅。

127
00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:39.190
It is covered in LED lights and Waterford crystal.
上面覆盖着LED灯和沃特福德水晶。

128
00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.110
Fancy.
真高级。

129
00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.430
Very fancy.
非常高级。

130
00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:42.650
So that's it.
所以就是这样。

131
00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.690
Those are your, like, little New Year's tidbits.
这些就是关于新年的一些小知识。

132
00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:50.510
You can bring those out at your party this year and sound very knowledgeable about the New Year.
今年参加派对时你可以拿出来显摆一下，显得你对新年很有研究。

133
00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.050
Well, I loved that, Jenna.
我很喜欢这些，珍娜。

134
00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.290
I loved every single second.
我喜欢每一秒钟。

135
