00:30:20.520 --> 00:30:21.920
We had a fan question.
我们有个粉丝提问。

608
00:30:22.660 --> 00:30:22.860
Okay.
好的。

609
00:30:22.860 --> 00:30:30.240
Allie Jo Higginbotham says, did Angela improv that line, I don't want these, to Pam, after
艾莉·乔·希金博瑟姆问，安吉拉，那句“我不想要这些”是你对帕姆即兴发挥的吗？是在

610
00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:31.360
she took the jelly beans?
她拿走软糖之后？

611
00:30:32.580 --> 00:30:33.000
Yes.
是的。

612
00:30:33.640 --> 00:30:34.580
Yes, I did.
没错，是我说的。

613
00:30:35.300 --> 00:30:40.520
The note that Greg had given me in that scene is that, you know, I'm so anxious to talk to
格雷格在那场戏里给我的指示是，你知道，我非常急切地想和

614
00:30:40.520 --> 00:30:42.280
Dwight to find out that everything went okay.
德怀特谈谈，确认一切都顺利。

615
00:30:42.280 --> 00:30:44.840
But I had to make some business for myself.
但我得给自己找点事做。

616
00:30:44.980 --> 00:30:46.200
Like, why would I be at reception?
比如，我为什么会在前台？

617
00:30:46.580 --> 00:30:49.160
So, I decided to kind of dig in the jelly beans.
所以我决定去翻翻那些软糖。

618
00:30:49.300 --> 00:30:51.360
I just sort of was like, oh, this is what I'll do.
我当时就想，哦，我就这么做吧。

619
00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:53.420
So, I was digging in the jelly beans.
于是我就在翻那些软糖。

620
00:30:53.540 --> 00:30:55.640
And I put a few in my hand throughout the scene.
在整场戏里，我往手里抓了几颗。

621
00:30:56.020 --> 00:30:58.600
And then as Dwight walked away, I just had them in my hand.
然后当德怀特走开时，我手里正好拿着它们。

622
00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.320
So, I just placed them on the countertop.
所以我就把它们放在了柜台上。

623
00:31:01.400 --> 00:31:02.220
Like your kid would.
就像小孩子会做的那样。

624
00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:03.220
I don't like this.
我不喜欢这个。

625
00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:04.000
Yes.
是的。

626
00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:04.900
He just walked away.
他直接走开了。

627
00:31:05.340 --> 00:31:07.660
And it just tickled us so much.
这把我们逗乐坏了。

628
00:31:07.680 --> 00:31:08.820
And they left it in.
而且他们把这一段留在了正片里。

629
00:31:08.820 --> 00:31:13.360
But the part I love even more, Jenna, is your look.
但珍娜，我更喜欢的是你的表情。

630
00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:18.100
Your look of like, it said so much to me in the moment.
你那种表情，在那一刻对我来说传达了太多信息。

631
00:31:18.280 --> 00:31:23.680
It said people leave their water bottles and their trash on my desk.
那表情仿佛在说，人们总是把水瓶和垃圾留在我的桌子上。

632
00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:24.860
All the time.
一直都是这样。

633
00:31:25.060 --> 00:31:29.260
After you would leave the jelly beans, I added a little bit that got cut out.
在你留下软糖之后，我还加了一点戏，不过被剪掉了。

634
00:31:29.400 --> 00:31:32.260
And probably it should have been cut out because it just would have gone on forever.
而且剪掉可能是对的，因为那段戏可能会没完没了。

635
00:31:32.260 --> 00:31:36.900
But I would find all these various ways to get rid of the jelly beans.
但我会想出各种各样的方法来处理掉那些软糖。

636
00:31:37.120 --> 00:31:42.420
So, I remember one time I picked up the trash can and I scooched them into the trash can using a piece of paper.
我记得有一次我拿起垃圾桶，用一张纸把它们扫进垃圾桶里。

637
00:31:42.680 --> 00:31:47.500
And another time I like took a tissue and I picked them up with a tissue.
还有一次我拿了张纸巾，用纸巾把它们捡起来。

638
00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:52.720
And another time I think I picked them up and put them back in the jelly bean container.
还有一次我想我是把它们捡起来放回了软糖罐子里。

639
00:31:52.720 --> 00:31:58.120
But I had, I know, I had all these ways that I got rid of these jelly beans.
总之，我知道我试过各种方法来处理这些软糖。

640
00:31:58.320 --> 00:32:00.100
And I had a good time with that.
我当时玩得很开心。

641
00:32:00.340 --> 00:32:01.620
None of them made it in, of course.
当然，这些都没能出现在正片里。

642
00:32:01.840 --> 00:32:05.200
But it was just kind of like a fun little bit we were doing.
但这只是我们当时玩的一个有趣的小桥段。

643
00:32:05.460 --> 00:32:08.240
So, should we move into the conference room now, Angela?
那么，安吉拉，我们现在该去会议室了吗？

644
00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:09.700
Oh, yeah.
哦，好的。

645
00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:12.820
Because somebody needs to pass the tarty sauce.
因为有人得递一下塔塔酱。

646
00:32:13.140 --> 00:32:13.600
Yes.
没错。

647
00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:18.240
The entire sales team is assembled in the conference room and Dwight comes in late.
整个销售团队都聚集在会议室里，而德怀特迟到了。

648
00:32:18.400 --> 00:32:20.560
So, Andy is such a tool.
安迪真是个十足的蠢货。

649
00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:21.680
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

650
00:32:21.680 --> 00:32:27.420
So, at the beginning of this scene, Michael explains that this is his dream team.
在这场戏的开头，迈克尔解释说这是他的梦之队。

651
00:32:27.420 --> 00:32:29.420
This is my dream sales team.
这就是我梦想中的销售团队。

652
00:32:29.420 --> 00:32:32.080
And we're going to pair up and go on some sales calls.
我们要两两分组，去跑几趟销售业务。

653
00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:35.960
And we had a fan question from Holly Enerson.
我们收到一个来自Holly Enerson的粉丝提问。

654
00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:44.800
Holly Enerson says, Phyllis blows her nose right after Michael says, this is my dream team.
Holly Enerson说，在迈克尔说完“这是我梦想中的团队”后，菲利斯立刻擤了鼻涕。

655
00:32:45.080 --> 00:32:46.800
Was that scripted?
那是剧本安排的吗？

656
00:32:46.960 --> 00:32:49.680
I wondered the same thing because it's brilliant.
我也纳闷呢，因为那简直神了。

657
00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:51.580
The timing is so perfect.
时机抓得太完美了。

658
00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:53.260
It's so perfect.
真是太完美了。

659
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:55.840
Yes, it was scripted.
是的，那是剧本写的。

660
00:32:56.080 --> 00:32:56.460
Amazing.
太棒了。

661
00:32:57.140 --> 00:32:58.800
Here is the script direction.
剧本说明是这样写的。

662
00:32:59.340 --> 00:33:03.660
Quote, the camera pans to bored faces of the sales team.
引用：镜头扫过销售团队成员们百无聊赖的脸。

663
00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:05.620
Phyllis blows her nose.
菲利斯擤了擤鼻涕。

664
00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:12.860
And, you know, guys, this is a little moment because I watched it several times.
而且，伙计们，这是一个很小的细节，因为我看了好几遍。

665
00:33:13.900 --> 00:33:15.040
It's so great.
真的太棒了。

666
00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:17.180
Phyllis gets out her little tissue.
菲利斯掏出她的小纸巾。

667
00:33:17.520 --> 00:33:19.240
She sniffles a little bit.
她吸了吸鼻子。

668
00:33:19.420 --> 00:33:20.960
And then she blows her nose.
然后擤了擤鼻涕。

669
00:33:21.400 --> 00:33:23.540
Like, she times it perfectly.
她掐的时间点简直完美。

670
00:33:23.540 --> 00:33:25.980
But she starts the bit a little early.
但她稍微提前了一点开始做这个动作。

671
00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:29.800
And I think that's what sells making it look so organic.
我觉得正是这一点让它看起来如此自然。

672
00:33:30.060 --> 00:33:32.160
It's really wonderful work.
这真的是非常精彩的表演。

673
00:33:32.300 --> 00:33:33.340
Little details.
小细节。

674
00:33:33.820 --> 00:33:35.880
Phyllis, man, with the tissue work.
菲利斯，天哪，那纸巾戏份。

675
00:33:35.880 --> 00:33:37.820
So everyone gets paired up.
所以每个人都两两分组了。

676
00:33:38.080 --> 00:33:38.660
Yes.
没错。

677
00:33:38.820 --> 00:33:46.280
We get Karen and Phyllis and Ryan and Stanley, Dwight and Jim and Michael and Andy.
凯伦和菲利斯一组，瑞安和斯坦利一组，德怀特和吉姆一组，迈克尔和安迪一组。

678
00:33:46.540 --> 00:33:50.060
Now they're going to go out and be in cars together all day.
现在他们要一起出门，整天待在车里了。

679
00:33:50.060 --> 00:33:51.040
I couldn't wait.
我简直等不及了。

680
00:33:51.220 --> 00:33:53.540
I remember when we got the script, Jenna, at the table read.
珍娜，我记得我们拿到剧本在围读的时候。

681
00:33:53.680 --> 00:33:57.640
When I saw, like, the groupings, I was like, oh, this is going to be so fun.
当我看到分组时，我就想，哦，这一定会很有趣。

682
00:33:57.980 --> 00:34:02.500
Well, there's a Ryan talking head in here that makes me laugh so hard.
对了，这里有个瑞安的采访镜头让我笑得不行。

683
00:34:02.740 --> 00:34:04.900
Because you are now Ryan in real life.
因为你现在在现实生活中就是瑞安。

684
00:34:04.940 --> 00:34:05.900
I am now Ryan.
我现在就是瑞安。

685
00:34:06.420 --> 00:34:11.640
I love it that he said he's flattered to be Stanley's second choice after pass.
他说自己很荣幸能成为斯坦利在“拒绝”之后的第二选择，我太喜欢这段了。

686
00:34:13.340 --> 00:34:14.220
After pass.
在“拒绝”之后。

687
00:34:14.820 --> 00:34:16.320
Stanley got to pick his partner.
斯坦利可以挑选他的搭档。

688
00:34:16.580 --> 00:34:18.580
And his first response was pass.
他的第一反应是拒绝。

689
00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:19.020
Pass.
拒绝。

690
00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:22.100
And his second response was, I guess I'll take the kid.
而他的第二反应是，好吧，我选这小子吧。

691
00:34:22.820 --> 00:34:26.240
Well, I wanted to talk really quickly about Jim's talking head.
对了，我想快速聊聊吉姆的采访镜头。

692
00:34:26.460 --> 00:34:30.320
He holds up that photo of Dwight and Jim, like the old photo.
他举起那张德怀特和吉姆的照片，就是那张旧照片。

693
00:34:30.520 --> 00:34:35.160
Because they clearly have been on a ton of sales calls together, right?
因为他们显然一起跑过很多次销售业务，对吧？

694
00:34:35.260 --> 00:34:38.420
And it shows their history a little bit, which I love.
这稍微展示了他们的过往，我非常喜欢。

695
00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:45.360
But in the DVD commentary, Rain said that his hair in that photo was from 1991.
但在DVD评论音轨里，雷恩说照片里他的发型是1991年的。

696
00:34:45.360 --> 00:34:52.360
He was on tour with an acting company doing Romeo and Juliet, and they all had long Elizabethan hair.
当时他正随一个剧团巡演《罗密欧与朱丽叶》，他们都留着伊丽莎白时代的长发。

697
00:34:55.720 --> 00:35:01.200
And they sort of, they sort of like photoshopped it onto current Dwight, but they left that big hair.
他们算是把那头长发P到了现在的德怀特身上，但保留了那头大长发。

698
00:35:01.340 --> 00:35:02.260
I just thought it was hilarious.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

699
00:35:02.260 --> 00:35:04.640
I love that detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

700
00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:05.660
I know.
我也是。

701
00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:08.180
So now they're all in the parking lot.
现在他们都到了停车场。

702
00:35:08.360 --> 00:35:09.460
They're paired up into their teaMs.
他们被分成了小组。

703
00:35:09.640 --> 00:35:11.180
They're about to get in their cars and go.
他们正准备上车出发。

704
00:35:11.820 --> 00:35:16.400
Michael tosses Dwight his dirty laundry, which is a callback to the coup.
迈克尔把脏衣服扔给德怀特，这是对之前政变情节的呼应。

705
00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:20.800
I love it when our show does this, and we have a few in this episode.
我喜欢我们剧集里的这种设计，这一集里有好几处。

706
00:35:20.980 --> 00:35:22.560
But this is a callback to the coup.
但这确实是对政变情节的呼应。

707
00:35:23.120 --> 00:35:27.200
And now he tells them all to circle up, and he's going to give them their marching orders.
现在他让大家围过来，准备下达行动指令。

708
00:35:27.960 --> 00:35:28.320
Yeah.
没错。

709
00:35:28.500 --> 00:35:33.040
So then Michael says, guys, let's go out on our sales calls.
迈克尔说，伙计们，我们去跑销售吧。

710
00:35:33.160 --> 00:35:35.320
This is, it's like the, we're the amazing race.
这感觉就像是……我们是在参加《极速前进》。

711
00:35:35.620 --> 00:35:38.180
And everyone's like, how are we the amazing race?
大家都一脸困惑，问怎么就成《极速前进》了？

712
00:35:38.220 --> 00:35:39.100
Is there a prize?
有奖金吗？

713
00:35:39.320 --> 00:35:40.580
He's like, no, there's no prize.
他说，没有，没奖金。

714
00:35:40.600 --> 00:35:42.400
But we're the amazing race.
但我们就是在参加《极速前进》。

715
00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:47.080
And he keeps, gives everybody these team names and everyone's very confused.
他不停地给每个人起队名，大家都感到非常困惑。

716
00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:48.960
And then Michael just gets frustrated.
然后迈克尔就变得沮丧起来。

717
00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:51.120
He's like, just go on your sales call.
他说，你们就去跑销售吧。

718
00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:54.480
But I love that he brought up the amazing race.
但我很喜欢他提到《极速前进》这一点。

719
00:35:54.780 --> 00:35:57.640
This was a really, really popular reality show at the time.
那可是当时非常、非常火的真人秀节目。

720
00:35:57.780 --> 00:35:59.300
And I was a huge fan.
我当时也是超级粉丝。

721
00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:01.780
Jenna, we were so into it.
珍娜，我们当时特别迷那个节目。

722
00:36:01.880 --> 00:36:03.920
I remember you and I watching the amazing race.
我还记得你和我一起看《极速前进》的情景。

723
00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:07.140
And then Jenna, do you remember how you and I were like, we should go on.
珍娜，你还记得我们当时说应该去参加吗？

724
00:36:07.320 --> 00:36:09.560
We should be a team on amazing race together.
我们应该一起组队去参加《极速前进》。

725
00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:11.220
I stand by that.
我依然坚持这个想法。

726
00:36:11.420 --> 00:36:12.060
I think we should.
我觉得我们应该去。

727
00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:14.420
I think we, we would have been amazing.
我觉得我们一定会表现得很棒。

728
00:36:14.980 --> 00:36:17.160
I think we would have been a total mess.
我觉得我们会彻底搞砸。

729
00:36:18.020 --> 00:36:18.380
Why?
为什么？

730
00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:19.620
Why?
为什么？

731
00:36:20.700 --> 00:36:23.760
Because I think you would be like, let's go, let's go.
因为我觉得你会一直催，快走，快走。

732
00:36:23.840 --> 00:36:25.220
And I'd be like, can we just take a break?
而我会说，我们能休息一下吗？

733
00:36:25.420 --> 00:36:26.500
Maybe we'll have a glass of wine.
也许我们该喝杯红酒。

734
00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:27.340
You'd be like, yeah, yeah.
你肯定会说，行吧，行吧。

735
00:36:28.840 --> 00:36:31.400
Also, I can't eat any of that gross stuff, lady.
而且，我可吃不了那些恶心的东西，大姐。

736
00:36:31.520 --> 00:36:32.660
I can't eat the gross stuff.
我吃不下那些恶心的东西。

737
00:36:33.060 --> 00:36:34.280
Well, this is the problem.
嗯，这就是问题所在。

738
00:36:34.460 --> 00:36:37.660
I think we would both have some of the same weaknesses.
我觉得我们俩会有一些共同的弱点。

739
00:36:38.060 --> 00:36:39.920
I think we couldn't eat the gross stuff.
我觉得我们都吃不下那些恶心的东西。

740
00:36:39.920 --> 00:36:45.520
And maybe neither one of us would have great upper body strength for some of the things
而且可能我们俩在上肢力量方面都不太行，应付不了某些任务，

741
00:36:45.520 --> 00:36:49.860
where you have to like, like toss bales of hay down a maze or something.
比如那种要把干草捆扔过迷宫之类的活儿。

742
00:36:50.140 --> 00:36:52.420
How about zero upper body strength?
上肢力量为零怎么样？

743
00:36:52.820 --> 00:36:53.000
Yeah.
没错。

744
00:36:53.460 --> 00:36:53.900
Like, zero.
就是零。

745
00:36:54.240 --> 00:36:57.500
So maybe we wouldn't have been such a great team, but we would have had fun.
所以也许我们成不了那么棒的队伍，但我们会玩得很开心。

746
00:36:58.140 --> 00:36:59.280
I think we would have had fun.
我觉得我们会玩得很开心。

747
00:36:59.380 --> 00:37:02.760
I think we would have had one colossal meltdown and then a fight.
我觉得我们会彻底崩溃，然后大吵一架。

748
00:37:02.800 --> 00:37:04.040
And then we would have cried.
接着我们会哭一场。

749
00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:06.000
And then we'd laugh hysterically.
然后又会歇斯底里地大笑。

750
00:37:06.200 --> 00:37:08.560
We'd look like crazy people.
看起来就像疯子一样。

751
00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:09.920
But we would have had fun.
但我们本来会玩得很开心的。

752
00:37:10.220 --> 00:37:12.160
I tell you what, we would have been good TV.
跟你说吧，我们本来会成为很好的电视节目的。

753
00:37:12.740 --> 00:37:13.640
Oh, my God.
天哪。

754
00:37:13.640 --> 00:37:15.060
We would have been great TV.
我们本来会成为很棒的电视节目的。

755
00:37:17.060 --> 00:37:17.800
OK, OK.
好吧，好吧。

756
00:37:17.980 --> 00:37:21.060
Well, we actually asked Greg about this Amazing Race moment.
其实我们问过格雷格关于这个《极速前进》桥段的事。

757
00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:22.460
And here's what he had to say.
听听他是怎么说的。

758
